Package: bayesianquilts
Title: Adaptive Importance Sampling and Quilted-Model Scaling for Bayesian Cross-Validation
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: person("Joshua", "Chang", email = "josh@mederrata.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: R port of the bayesianquilts library for interpretable Bayesian machine learning.
    Provides Adaptive Importance Sampling (AIS) methods for efficient Leave-One-Out (LOO)
    cross-validation, with support for brms models and custom likelihood functions.
    Includes the full-rank transformations MM3 and PMM3, the natural-gradient variants
    NLD and NKL, the variance-based transformation, and MixIS (Silva & Zanella 2024).
    Also provides the quilted-model interaction decomposition with the manuscript's
    generalization-preserving prior scales (Chang 2025) so multi-way component priors
    can be set from data marginals.
